[
    {
        "content": "<p>In <a href=\"https://github.com/suhr/iris-tutorial\">https://github.com/suhr/iris-tutorial</a> I started to port iris-tutorial to Lean. Here's some problems met so far:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>You can't write <code>⊢ P -∗ (P -∗ Q) -∗ Q</code> as simply <code>P -∗ (P -∗ Q) -∗ Q</code> in iris-lean</li>\n<li>The tutorial needs <code>iapply</code> but there's no such tactic in iris-lean yet</li>\n</ul>",
        "id": 528528122,
        "sender_full_name": "suhr",
        "timestamp": 1752411355
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"394485\">suhr</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/490604-iris-lean/topic/Porting.20iris-tutorial/near/528528122\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<ul>\n<li>You can't write <code>⊢ P -∗ (P -∗ Q) -∗ Q</code> as simply <code>P -∗ (P -∗ Q) -∗ Q</code> in iris-lean</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I think this is not likely to get better. You could get <code>iprop(P -∗ (P -∗ Q) -∗ Q)</code> to work but that's not really better.</p>",
        "id": 528991590,
        "sender_full_name": "Mario Carneiro",
        "timestamp": 1752648728
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I tired of waiting for <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/iris-lean/pull/80\">https://github.com/leanprover-community/iris-lean/pull/80</a> to be merged, so I filled the rest of <code>Basics.lean</code> using a fork of the repo.</p>\n<p>There are three unproven lemmas remaining, which use <code>⊣⊢</code>. In the tutorial, bi-entails is split with <code>iSplit</code>, but in iris-lean <code>isplit</code>  does not work for <code>⊣⊢</code>.</p>",
        "id": 544319237,
        "sender_full_name": "suhr",
        "timestamp": 1760187429
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>But <code>constructor</code> works fine for <code>⊣⊢</code></p>",
        "id": 546685321,
        "sender_full_name": "suhr",
        "timestamp": 1761227385
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Now I'm trying to port <code>pure.v</code>, but <code>theorem eq_elm {A} (P : A → iProp σ) (x y : A) : (⌜x = y⌝ : IProp σ) -∗ P x -∗ P y := sorry</code> gives me the following error: <code>error: IrisTutorial/Pure.lean:39:49: elaboration function for 'Iris.BI.BIBase.«term_-∗_»' has not been implemented</code>.</p>",
        "id": 546696461,
        "sender_full_name": "suhr",
        "timestamp": 1761229894
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think you should put your main goal a <code>⊢</code>. Enclosing it in <code>iprop(...)</code> might also work.</p>",
        "id": 546907464,
        "sender_full_name": "Markus de Medeiros",
        "timestamp": 1761315096
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Huh, I forgot about the <code>⊢</code>  thing again. Thanks!</p>",
        "id": 546911176,
        "sender_full_name": "suhr",
        "timestamp": 1761315996
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Now both <code>basics.v</code> and <code>pure.v</code> are ported, and the rest of tutorial requires heaplang.</p>",
        "id": 546919149,
        "sender_full_name": "suhr",
        "timestamp": 1761318144
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Now we have some bits of HeapLang, so I tried to update iris-lean in iris-tutorial. Unfortunately, some proof that used to work does not work anymore.</p>\n<p>Specifically, this used to work:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sep_ex_distr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IProp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IProp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∗</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊣⊢</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∗</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">constructor</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">iintro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">hp</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fx</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">iexists</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">isplitl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">hp</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">iexact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hp</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">iexact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fx</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">iintro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hp</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fx</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">isplitl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">hp</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">iexact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hp</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">iexists</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">iexact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fx</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>But with current iris-lean <code>iintro</code> fails with <code>icases: cannot destruct iprop(∃ x, Φ x)</code>.</p>\n<p>How to fix this proof?</p>",
        "id": 591155703,
        "sender_full_name": "suhr",
        "timestamp": 1777300802
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>By the way, <code>iapply pqr with p, q</code> does not work anymore either, so I had to use</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">iapply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pqr</span>\n<span class=\"n\">isplitl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">iexact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">iexact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>which is a bit more annoying.</p>",
        "id": 591156622,
        "sender_full_name": "suhr",
        "timestamp": 1777301001
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think the syntax for term application has changed, and now it uses <code>$$</code> instead of <code>with</code></p>",
        "id": 591157232,
        "sender_full_name": "Fernando LEAL",
        "timestamp": 1777301134
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Have you tried <code>iapply pqr $$ [p] [q]</code>? Or something along those lines</p>",
        "id": 591157287,
        "sender_full_name": "Fernando LEAL",
        "timestamp": 1777301148
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This fails with <code>ispecialize: R is not a wand</code>.</p>",
        "id": 591157993,
        "sender_full_name": "suhr",
        "timestamp": 1777301315
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>By the way, here's the PR: <a href=\"https://github.com/suhr/iris-tutorial/pull/1\">https://github.com/suhr/iris-tutorial/pull/1</a>. I plan to port other parts of iris-tutorial, but I need to fix the proof of <code>sep_ex_distr</code> first.</p>",
        "id": 591158797,
        "sender_full_name": "suhr",
        "timestamp": 1777301520
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"394485\">suhr</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/490604-iris-lean/topic/Porting.20iris-tutorial/near/591155703\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Now we have some bits of HeapLang, so I tried to update iris-lean in iris-tutorial. Unfortunately, some proof that used to work does not work anymore.</p>\n<p>Specifically, this used to work:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sep_ex_distr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IProp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IProp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∗</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊣⊢</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∗</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">constructor</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">iintro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">hp</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fx</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">iexists</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">isplitl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">hp</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">iexact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hp</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">iexact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fx</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">iintro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hp</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fx</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">isplitl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">hp</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">iexact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hp</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">iexists</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">iexact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fx</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>But with current iris-lean <code>iintro</code> fails with <code>icases: cannot destruct iprop(∃ x, Φ x)</code>.</p>\n<p>How to fix this proof?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>change the <code>x</code> to <code>%x</code> should fix it</p>",
        "id": 591159212,
        "sender_full_name": "Alex Bai",
        "timestamp": 1777301628
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It does! Thanks.</p>",
        "id": 591159639,
        "sender_full_name": "suhr",
        "timestamp": 1777301738
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>When the proof mode is more stabilized, maybe having a file like <a href=\"https://gitlab.mpi-sws.org/iris/iris/-/blob/master/docs/proof_mode.md\">https://gitlab.mpi-sws.org/iris/iris/-/blob/master/docs/proof_mode.md</a> will be helpful</p>",
        "id": 591159844,
        "sender_full_name": "Alex Bai",
        "timestamp": 1777301783
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>There's <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/iris-lean/blob/master/Iris/tactics.md\">https://github.com/leanprover-community/iris-lean/blob/master/Iris/tactics.md</a>, but it's not very detailed, and error messages are a bit cryptic.</p>",
        "id": 591160574,
        "sender_full_name": "suhr",
        "timestamp": 1777301951
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If you have suggestions for ways that document could be improved (ie. cryptic errors you deciphered) please feel free to drop them here!</p>",
        "id": 591168830,
        "sender_full_name": "Markus de Medeiros",
        "timestamp": 1777303865
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Well, for example, <code>icases: cannot destruct iprop(∃ x, Φ x)</code> does not tell <em>why</em> it can't destruct <code>iprop(∃ x, Φ x)</code>. It could at least tell something about <code>x</code> being pure. Even better if it suggested using <code>%x</code> right away.</p>",
        "id": 591172901,
        "sender_full_name": "suhr",
        "timestamp": 1777305029
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Now I'm porting HeapLang specifications, and have the following problem. I have this code and spec:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">arith</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Exp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hl</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">arith_spec</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊢@</span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">IProp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">GF</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">WP</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">arith</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⌜</span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hl_val</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"mi\">16</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">⌝</span><span class=\"o\">}}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">unfold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">arith</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">istart</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">wp_pures</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>As I understand, <code>wp_pures</code> should evaluate pure expressions inside a heaplang expression. But for some reason in this expression it does not evaluate anything.</p>",
        "id": 602747957,
        "sender_full_name": "suhr",
        "timestamp": 1781330097
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"394485\">@suhr</span> I ran into this too. I think more instances of Language.PureExec need to be added/generalized. Right now it looks like the only pure binary op we support is ≤. (see <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/iris-lean/blob/b7161660991216899f212eb33a9da47418655404/Iris/Iris/HeapLang/Instances.lean#L173\">https://github.com/leanprover-community/iris-lean/blob/b7161660991216899f212eb33a9da47418655404/Iris/Iris/HeapLang/Instances.lean#L173</a>).</p>",
        "id": 602756768,
        "sender_full_name": "Paul Berry",
        "timestamp": 1781333475
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I see. By the way, it seems like this file need a bit of clean up, there's a lot of repetition.</p>",
        "id": 602768112,
        "sender_full_name": "suhr",
        "timestamp": 1781337088
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah, it does seem like we could de-duplicate a lot of that file, either with a side lemma or maybe a bit of metaprogramming.</p>",
        "id": 602805496,
        "sender_full_name": "Paul Berry",
        "timestamp": 1781349125
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>We should definitely fill in the rest of that file!</p>",
        "id": 602805715,
        "sender_full_name": "Markus de Medeiros",
        "timestamp": 1781349194
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Personally I don't think I'd bother with metaprogramming it because it just needs to be done once, and the examples sadly aren't all just copy/paste. But if there's something slick then sure</p>",
        "id": 602805936,
        "sender_full_name": "Markus de Medeiros",
        "timestamp": 1781349265
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Sorry I completely missed this! I also started a port of the tutorial (mostly Claude translated) at <a href=\"https://github.com/logsem/iris-tutorial-lean/\">https://github.com/logsem/iris-tutorial-lean/</a>. In this port I'm trying to use the Verso framework, and I think it works pretty well. See e.g. <a href=\"https://logsem.github.io/iris-tutorial-lean/Basics-of-Iris/Basic-Separation-Logic/#The-Iris-Tutorial-in-Lean--Basics-of-Iris--Basic-Separation-Logic\">https://logsem.github.io/iris-tutorial-lean/Basics-of-Iris/Basic-Separation-Logic/#The-Iris-Tutorial-in-Lean--Basics-of-Iris--Basic-Separation-Logic</a>. I think it’s fine to keep the multiple ports if you’re doing this for learning but otherwise we should coordinate to avoid duplication.</p>",
        "id": 602871341,
        "sender_full_name": "Zongyuan Liu",
        "timestamp": 1781371011
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"1080689\">Paul Berry</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/490604-iris-lean/topic/Porting.20iris-tutorial/near/602756768\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I think more instances of Language.PureExec need to be added/generalized.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Indeed, you are correct. I created <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/iris-lean/pull/463\">https://github.com/leanprover-community/iris-lean/pull/463</a> which adds the missing instances.</p>",
        "id": 602887345,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Sammler",
        "timestamp": 1781376272
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"883069\">Zongyuan Liu</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/490604-iris-lean/topic/Porting.20iris-tutorial/near/602871341\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I think it’s fine to keep the multiple ports if you’re doing this for learning but otherwise we should coordinate to avoid duplication.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I indeed do it for learning and also to see what's missing (or painful) in Iris-Lean. By the way, set <code>htmlDepth := 1</code> in verso, so the tutorial would be easier to navigate.</p>",
        "id": 602973888,
        "sender_full_name": "suhr",
        "timestamp": 1781408498
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I believe there's no reason to hurry porting iris-tutorial, because it's mostly blocked by Iris-Lean rather than by writing. For the same reason I did not try to set up Verso in my repository.</p>",
        "id": 602978427,
        "sender_full_name": "suhr",
        "timestamp": 1781410339
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Also, <code>The Rocq tutorial begins with ... The Lean version of these tactics is ...</code> is extremely awkward. My plan was to port iris-lean verbatim first, and when it's ready, write a Iris-Lean native tutorial without explicit references to the Rocq tutorial.</p>\n<p>Now I think this can be done incrementally chapter by chapter. But could we please avoid that mixed Rocq-Lean prose?</p>",
        "id": 602980357,
        "sender_full_name": "suhr",
        "timestamp": 1781411014
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"394485\">suhr</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/490604-iris-lean/topic/Porting.20iris-tutorial/near/602978427\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I believe there's no reason to hurry porting iris-tutorial, because it's mostly blocked by Iris-Lean rather than by writing. For the same reason I did not try to set up Verso in my repository.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>My main motivations were to play with Verso and figure out what are still missing in Iris-Lean for the tutorial. Please ignore the prose for now. I agree that we should have a version that is tailored for Lean.</p>",
        "id": 603063545,
        "sender_full_name": "Zongyuan Liu",
        "timestamp": 1781443313
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"394485\">@suhr</span> I'd take the <del>\"Persistently\"</del> \"Later\" section. <br>\nIIUC you're currently at \"Specifications\", and since there is progress on porting <code>wp_*</code> tactics recently, I guess you can finish it soon.<br>\nUPD: seems like the next chapter not covered by you or <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"883069\">@Zongyuan Liu</span>  is \"Later\", so I'd rather take that. <br>\nAre there any plans on merging the two tutorials?</p>",
        "id": 610783288,
        "sender_full_name": "Egor Namakonov",
        "timestamp": 1784115920
    },
    {
        "content": "<blockquote>\n<p>IIUC you're currently at \"Specifications\", and since there is progress on porting <code>wp_*</code> tactics recently, I guess you can finish it soon.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Tactics are not a problem, you can just apply the primitive rules. For example:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cmpXchg_0_to_10_spec</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Loc</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Val</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-∗</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">WP</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">cmpXchg_0_to_10</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">⌜</span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hl_val</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">⌝</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∗</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hl_val</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"mi\">10</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∨</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                                </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">⌜</span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≠</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hl_val</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">⌝</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∗</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">}}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">unfold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cmpXchg_0_to_10</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">aa</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ProgramLogic</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toVal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hl</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">some</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hl_val</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bb</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ProgramLogic</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toVal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hl</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"mi\">10</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">some</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hl_val</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"mi\">10</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hv</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hl_val</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">hv</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hl_val</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">compareSafe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hl_val</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">iintro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hl</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">iapply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">wp_cmpXchg_true'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">aa</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bb</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$$</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hl</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v''</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">iintro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">ha</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hb</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">ileft</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">iframe</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">ipureintro</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">else</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">iintro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hl</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">compareSafe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hl_val</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hl_val</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isUnboxed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Val</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">compareSafe</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">this</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">iapply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">wp_cmpXchg_fail'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">aa</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bb</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">cc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">decide_eq_false</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hv</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$$</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hl</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v''</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">iintro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">ha</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hb</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">iright</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">iframe</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">ipureintro</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hv</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Here I used different versions of <code>wp_cmpXchg_true</code> and <code>wp_cmpXchg_fail</code>, which are more friendly to <code>iapply</code>.</p>\n<p>The problem so far is I simply don't have enough time to work on iris-tutorial right now.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Are there any plans on merging the two tutorials?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>That's possible, but I really would like to leave the original prose intact instead of translating it with AI.</p>",
        "id": 610803381,
        "sender_full_name": "suhr",
        "timestamp": 1784121211
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"394485\">suhr</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/490604-iris-lean/topic/Porting.20iris-tutorial/near/610803381\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>That's possible, but I really would like to leave the original prose intact instead of translating it with AI.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I don't see why you wanted to have the original prose for the Lean version. As I said before, I'm more than happy to have a manual rewriting of the prose tailored to Lean, if someone has some cycles to do it.</p>",
        "id": 610815327,
        "sender_full_name": "Zongyuan Liu",
        "timestamp": 1784123993
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"394485\">suhr</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/490604-iris-lean/topic/Porting.20iris-tutorial/near/610803381\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>That's possible, but I really would like to leave the original prose intact instead of translating it with AI.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Yes, I feel like the best version is to start with the original prose and edit it to suit Iris-Lean.</p>",
        "id": 610830613,
        "sender_full_name": "Markus de Medeiros",
        "timestamp": 1784127396
    }
]